@host = http://localhost:5045

### 1. Register a farmer (FR-01) -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ali Yilmaz",
  "email": "ali@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "role": "Farmer"
}

### 2. Register a consumer (FR-01) -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ayse Demir",
  "email": "ayse@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "role": "Consumer"
}

### 3. Log in as the farmer (FR-01) -> 200
# @name farmerLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ali@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### 4. Create a listing as the farmer (FR-02) -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/listings
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Tomato",
  "category": "vegetables",
  "unitPrice": 25.00,
  "unit": "kg",
  "availableQuantity": 50,
  "location": "İzmir"
}

### 5. Search listings (FR-03)
GET {{host}}/api/listings?search=tomato

### 6. Log in as the consumer
# @name consumerLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ayse@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### 7. Consumer tries to create a listing (NFR-03) -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/listings
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Apple",
  "category": "fruits",
  "unitPrice": 30.00,
  "unit": "kg",
  "availableQuantity": 20,
  "location": "Antalya"
}

### 8. Wrong password -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ali@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 9. Invalid listing data -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/listings
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "",
  "category": "vegetables",
  "unitPrice": -5,
  "unit": "kg",
  "availableQuantity": 0,
  "location": "İzmir"
}

### 10. Farmer creates a listing for the order tests (50 kg) -> 201
# @name orderListing
POST {{host}}/api/listings
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"productName": "Cucumber",
  
"category": "vegetables",
  
"unitPrice": 20.00,
  
"unit": "kg",
  
"availableQuantity": 50,
  
"location": "İzmir"
}
### 11. Consumer orders 10 kg (FR-04, FR-05) -> 201, remainingQuantity 40
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  
"quantity": 10,
  
"deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}

### 12. Quantity 0 (NFR-02) -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  
"quantity": 0,
  
"deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}

### 13. Quantity -1 (NFR-02) -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  
"quantity": -1,
  
"deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}


### 14. More than the stock: 41 kg when 40 kg is left (NFR-02) -> 400, stock stays 40
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  
"quantity": 41,
  
"deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}

### 15. Farmer tries to place an order (NFR-03) -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  
"quantity": 1,
  
"deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}

### 16. Order without logging in -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  
"quantity": 1,
  
"deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}

### 17. Listing that does not exist -> 404
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
  
"listingId": 99999,
  
"quantity": 1,
  
"deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}

### 18. Check the stock after the tests -> availableQuantity 40
GET {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}

### 19. Consumer places a new order for the status tests -> 201
# @name newOrder
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  "quantity": 2,
  "deliveryAddress": "Kadikoy, Istanbul"
}

### 20. Consumer sees own orders -> 200, newest first, status "pending"
GET {{host}}/api/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 21. Farmer sees received orders (FR-06) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/orders/received
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}


### 22. Farmer moves the order to Preparing (FR-06) -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{newOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "preparing"
}

### 23. Farmer moves it back to Pending -> 400 (status only moves forward)
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{newOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "pending"
}

### 24. Consumer tries to change the status (NFR-03) -> 403
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{newOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "delivered"
}

### 25. Register a second farmer -> 200 (409 if it already exists)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Mehmet Kaya",
  "email": "mehmet@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "role": "farmer"
}

### 26. Log in as the second farmer
# @name otherFarmerLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mehmet@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### 27. Second farmer tries to change Ali's order (NFR-03) -> 403
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{newOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{otherFarmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "delivered"
}

### 28. Farmer marks the order as Delivered (FR-06) -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{newOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "delivered"
}

### 29. Consumer checks again -> the order is now "delivered"
GET {{host}}/api/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 30. Farmer's own listings with order counts -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/listings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}


### 31. Consumer places a new 5 kg order to edit and cancel -> 201
# @name editOrder
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "listingId": {{orderListing.response.body.$.id}},
  "quantity": 5,
  "deliveryAddress": "Bakirkoy, Istanbul"
}

### 32. Consumer changes the order to 8 kg and a new address (FR-07) -> 200, stock 3 kg lower
PUT {{host}}/api/orders/{{editOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 8,
  "deliveryAddress": "Kadikoy, Istanbul"
}

### 33. Edit with quantity 0 (NFR-02) -> 400
PUT {{host}}/api/orders/{{editOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 0,
  "deliveryAddress": "Kadikoy, Istanbul"
}

### 34. Farmer: number of new orders (FR-09) -> 200, 1 or more
GET {{host}}/api/orders/received/unseen-count
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 35. Farmer: newest unseen orders (max 5) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/orders/received/unseen
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 36. Farmer opens the bell -> 204
POST {{host}}/api/orders/received/mark-seen
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 37. Count again -> 200, 0
GET {{host}}/api/orders/received/unseen-count
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 38. Consumer cancels the order (FR-08) -> 200, status "cancelled", 8 kg back to stock
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{editOrder.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 39. Cancel the same order again -> 409
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{editOrder.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 40. Edit a cancelled order -> 409
PUT {{host}}/api/orders/{{editOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 8,
  "deliveryAddress": "Kadikoy, Istanbul"
}

### 41. Farmer tries to move a cancelled order to Preparing -> 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{editOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "preparing"
}

### 42. Check the stock is back -> availableQuantity same as before test 31
GET {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}


### 43. City list from the database (FR-11) -> 200, 81 cities
GET {{host}}/api/cities

### 44. Farmer opens the edit form of an own listing (FR-10) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}/edit
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 45. Farmer changes price, stock and city (FR-10) -> 200
PUT {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Cucumber",
  "category": "vegetables",
  "unitPrice": 22.50,
  "unit": "kg",
  "availableQuantity": 60,
  "location": "Manisa"
}

### 46. City that is not in the list -> 400
PUT {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Cucumber",
  "category": "vegetables",
  "unitPrice": 22.50,
  "unit": "kg",
  "availableQuantity": 60,
  "location": "Atlantis"
}

### 47. Category that is not in the fixed list -> 400
PUT {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Cucumber",
  "category": "meat",
  "unitPrice": 22.50,
  "unit": "kg",
  "availableQuantity": 60,
  "location": "Manisa"
}

### 48. Change the unit of a listing that already has orders -> 400
PUT {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Cucumber",
  "category": "vegetables",
  "unitPrice": 22.50,
  "unit": "box",
  "availableQuantity": 60,
  "location": "Manisa"
}

### 49. Consumer tries to open the edit form (NFR-03) -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}/edit
Authorization: Bearer {{consumerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 50. Upload a text file as the photo (FR-12) -> 400
PUT {{host}}/api/listings/{{orderListing.response.body.$.id}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{farmerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=CropBoundary

--CropBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

this is not a photo
--CropBoundary--
